(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2609062230-x402-qr-ticket-platform-and-growth-profile")
  (:adr/title "x402 QR ticket checkout and Cloud Itonami global growth profile")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-06")
  (:adr/body "Owner requested kiosk QR payment design/implementation and a global-expansion Bot profile repository. nexus-x402 adds a merchant-presented QR lane with server-owned SKU terms, an order-specific EIP-3009 nonce, merchant-scoped SQLite Durable Objects, durable settlement reservation, and stable issuance IDs. Legacy KV spend accounting is not reused for ticket serialization. Unknown settlement never automatically retries. Terminal access is separate from checkout access. Physical issuance needs a machine-specific durable adapter and qualification. Compatibility implementation uses cljc state rules and ClojureScript Workers/browser hosts; it is not a claim of native Kotoba host parity. cloud-itonami/loop-x402-qr-growth carries the closed Cloud Itonami repo-profile schema, a bounded public observation script, country research hypotheses, and evidence/authority rules. Profile registration grants no funds, outreach, credentials, schedule, or deployment authority. Unit contract: 4 tests/27 assertions passed. Actual workerd SQLite/RPC integration passes 12 concurrent create/pay/claim requests, isolation, immutable terms, replay, ack, and uncertain settlement with a simulated upstream/printer. Mainnet transfer, physical printing, country admission, and external demand remain unverified. Deployment and runtime provisioning status are recorded separately in the affected repositories.")))
